            <ArticleTitle>Prognostic significance of angina pectoris &gt; or = 30 days before acute myocardial infarction in patients &gt; or = 75 years of age.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>198-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We compared the prognostic significance of prior angina pectoris in 151 patients &gt; or = 75 years of age admitted for acute myocardial infarction. There was a similar in-hospital course, but the long-term outcome was poorer in patients with prior angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
